Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: create a legacy context before opening GDI allocations

GDI devices can present without a user-mode driver issuing VIOGPU_CTX_INIT.
Their allocations were never attached to a host context, yet the BLT path
submitted a virgl RESOURCE_COPY_REGION on the device's allocated context ID.
After reboot, vmlab-hv correctly rejected these transfers and submissions.

Create the default legacy context when the kernel device is constructed.
Allocation opens can then attach their resources before the first present.
The existing Init path replaces this context when a UMD selects Venus or
another capset, and the destructor releases it through the existing path.
Device creation also requires initialized hardware, because it now queues
the context creation immediately.

The changed upstream file retains its MPL-2.0 licence.
---
diff --git a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_device.cpp b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_device.cpp
--- a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_device.cpp
+++ b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_device.cpp
@@ -23,7 +23,11 @@ VioGpuDevice::VioGpuDevice(VioGpuAdapter *pAdapter)
     ObReferenceObject(m_owner_process);
     m_id = pAdapter->ctxIdr.GetId();
     m_capset_id = 0;
-    m_context_created = false;
+    // GDI devices may present without a UMD context-init escape.
+    // Create their legacy context before allocations are opened.
+    // Init replaces it when a UMD requests another capset.
+    m_pAdapter->ctrlQueue.CreateCtx(m_id, 0);
+    m_context_created = true;
 }
 
 VioGpuDevice::~VioGpuDevice()
diff --git a/viogpu/viogpu3d/driver.cpp b/viogpu/viogpu3d/driver.cpp
--- a/viogpu/viogpu3d/driver.cpp
+++ b/viogpu/viogpu3d/driver.cpp
@@ -973,7 +973,7 @@ VioGpu3DCreateDevice(_In_ CONST HANDLE hAdapter, _Inout_ DXGKARG_CREATEDEVICE *pCreateDevice)
     DbgPrint(TRACE_LEVEL_VERBOSE, ("<---> %s\n", __FUNCTION__));
 
     VioGpuAdapter *pAdapter = reinterpret_cast<VioGpuAdapter *>(hAdapter);
-    if (!pAdapter->IsDriverActive())
+    if (!pAdapter->IsDriverActive() || !pAdapter->IsHardwareInit())
     {
         DbgPrint(TRACE_LEVEL_ERROR,
                  ("<---> %s VioGpu (%p) is being called when not active!\n", __FUNCTION__, pAdapter));
